                    $scController->cancelExcessScheduledSessions((int) $member->ID, $newTotal);
                    $scController->extendSessionsIfNeeded($member, $newTotal);
```

**`StudentClass.week` / `resolveScheduleSlotsForRebuild` (lines ~3103+)**  
Slots use **weekday in the range 1–7**; values **&lt; 1 or &gt; 7 are skipped**. From `buildSessionsForCount` (lines **3407–3408**), keys are matched to Carbon **`dayOfWeekIso`** (ISO-8601: **1 = Monday … 7 = Sunday**). So stored `week` / `week1`… values are **not** “0 = Monday”; **valid schedule weekdays are 1–7 with 1 = Monday and 7 = Sunday**.

```3107:3140:/home/admin/backend/app/Http/Controllers/StudentClassController.php
        if (!empty($providedSlots)) {
            foreach ($providedSlots as $slot) {
                $weekday = (int) ($slot['weekday'] ?? 0);
                if ($weekday < 1 || $weekday > 7) {
                    continue;
                }
                // ...
            }
        }
        // ...
                $weekday = (int) ($studentClass->{$weekField} ?? 0);
                if ($weekday < 1 || $weekday > 7) {
                    continue;
                }
```

```3406:3408:/home/admin/backend/app/Http/Controllers/StudentClassController.php
            $isoDow = (int) $dateObj->dayOfWeekIso;
            $daySlots = $slotsByWeekday[$isoDow] ?? [['time' => $firstTime]];
```

The `StudentClass` model docblock for `resolveSessionDurationForWeekday` also states **`1=Mon … 7=Sun`** (lines **73–74** in `/home/admin/backend/app/Models/StudentClass.php`).

